  "compare": "exact",
  "tests": {
    "visible": [
      {
        "label": "Standard RPN expression",
        "args": [
          [
            "2",
            "1",
            "+",
            "3",
            "*"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": 9
      },
      {
        "label": "Truncating negative division toward zero",
        "args": [
          [
            "10",
            "6",
            "9",
            "3",
            "+",
            "-11",
            "*",
            "/",
            "*",
            "17",
            "+",
            "5",
            "+"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": 22
      }
    ],
    "hidden": [
      {
        "label": "Single literal operand",
        "args": [
          [
            "42"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": 42
      },
      {
        "label": "Subtraction order b - a vs a - b",
        "args": [
          [
            "10",
            "3",
            "-"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": 7
      },
      {
        "label": "Negative dividend truncates toward zero (-7 / 2 == -3)",
        "args": [
          [
            "-7",
            "2",
            "/"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": -3
      },
      {
        "label": "Division positive truncation",
        "args": [
          [
            "7",
            "2",
            "/"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": 3
      },
      {
        "label": "Chained operators with negative result",
        "args": [
          [
            "5",
            "1",
            "2",
            "+",
            "4",
            "*",
            "+",
            "3",
            "-",
            "-1",
            "*"
          ]
        ],
        "expected": -14
      }
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Push integer operands onto a stack. When you see +, -, *, /, pop `right` first, then `left`!",
    "Division truncates toward zero (`int(left / right)`), NOT Python floor division `left // right` (since `-7 // 2 == -4` while `int(-7 / 2) == -3`).",
    "Pseudocode:\n  for tok in tokens:\n      if tok in {\"+\",\"-\",\"*\",\"/\"}:\n          b, a = stack.pop(), stack.pop()\n          apply op (use int(a / b) for \"/\")\n      else: stack.append(int(tok))\n  return stack[-1]"
  ],
